.TH MAGUS-STATUS 1 "" "magus" "magus Manual"
.SH NAME
magus\-status \- Inspect concurrency pool and configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magus
.RI "status [flags]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the magus configuration that affects this process \- telemetry, cache
settings \- and, when a parent magus process is running, the live state of its
concurrency pool (current slot usage, queued waiters).
.PP
When \-\-watch is non\-zero, status polls and reprints at that interval. On a
TTY the screen is cleared between reprints; piped output appends each
snapshot on its own line for log capture.
.PP
\-\-wait prints no snapshot: it exits 0 once this machine's build budget can
seat a run, and it is how a run refused with MGS3009 waits without a retry
loop. Piped into a magus run (magus status \-\-wait | magus run test .) it reads
that run's command from the pipe, waits until the budget can seat the claims
that run will make, and holds the run from starting until it exits; the run
then proceeds as usual, or starts nothing (MGS3030) if the wait failed. On
its own it waits for a free slot. A claim larger than the whole budget exits
78 at once; no broker means nothing to wait for, and it exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.RS
.TP
\fB\-W\fR \fIduration\fR
Short for \-\-watch
.TP
\fB\-c\fR
Short for \-\-compact
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
Single\-line, densely\-packed snapshot for sidebar/multiplexer use (text output only)
.TP
\fB\-\-probe\fR \fIstring\fR
Exec\-probe mode: liveness or readiness (exit 0 healthy, 1 unhealthy; ignores \-\-watch/\-\-compact)
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIstring\fR
Proc server to report on, as a unix:// URL or bare path; default: MAGUS_PROC_SOCKET inside a run, else every live one in the socket dir. \-\-probe asks the server at server.address unless this names one
.TP
\fB\-\-symbols\fR
Include the expensive symbol\-index freshness scan
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Exit 0 once the build budget can seat the magus run reading this pipe (a free slot when none does); holds that run until then
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR \fIduration\fR
Poll and reprint at this interval (minimum 15s; 0 means one\-shot)
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fIstring\fR
Workspace root to check for readiness with \-\-probe=readiness (default: any loaded workspace)
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
\fIOne\-shot status snapshot\fR
.PP
.EX
magus status
.EE
.PP
\fIRun tests once the build budget can seat them\fR
.PP
.EX
magus status --wait | magus run test .
.EE
.PP
\fILive updates every 15 seconds\fR
.PP
.EX
magus status --watch=15s
.EE
.PP
\fISingle\-line snapshot for a multiplexer sidebar\fR
.PP
.EX
magus status --compact --watch=15s
.EE
.PP
\fIInspect a specific running parent\fR
.PP
.EX
magus status --socket=unix:///run/user/1000/magus/server.sock
.EE
.PP
